==Strategy==
It is highly recommended to unlock the Target Angel [[Talents|talent]] on [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]] if you haven't already, as the Divine Cyclones become a cakewalk. The main threats here are the Traitless enemies, who can easily decimate everything while hiding behind the Cyclones.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Talents|Talented]] [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]] - Can efficiently crowd-control all three Divine Cyclones, but he's vulnerable to attacks from peons.
*[[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] - Can crowd-control all enemies here from afar and deal small amount of damage to Camelle, whom can cause issues if you don't have any sufficiently tanky or ranged units to counteract it, while inflicting slowness on all other enemies.
*[[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Gross]] - One of the earliest accessible Wave units, Crazed Gross has better chances of wiping the peons from a distance by abusing the durable Divine Cyclones to repeatedly launch Wave Attacks.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*Any [[EPICFEST (Gacha Event)|EPICFEST]] units will easily shred the support enemies and allow your stack to survive. Though most have to be supported to work, they absolutely delete the Rain Ds and Camelle.

==Trivia==
*Although its English name starts with a "D", Divine Cyclone appears in stages called [[Wrath of A-Cyclone (Insane)|Wrath of A-Cyclone]] and [[Revenge of A-Cyclone (Deadly)|Revenge of A-Cyclone]]. This is likely attributable to poor localization, since [[Divine Cyclone]]'s Japanese name is Angel Cyclone.

